From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ExposureMG <exposuremg@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:32:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] panvk: add Windows support

- Expose VK_KHR_win32_surface. Presentation uses the existing win32 WSI
  CPU path (GPU blit to a host-visible buffer, then a GDI blit).
- Get the device numbers of the synthetic render node from libdrm-win
  (they key the shared memory budget), and don't expose
  VK_EXT_physical_device_drm.
- Don't expose the fd/dma-buf external memory, semaphore and fence
  extensions, nor VK_EXT_map_memory_placed: there are no such fds, and the
  kernel driver creates CPU mappings itself.
- Build vulkan_panfrost.dll with the vk_icd* exports from vulkan_api.def
  and a backslash ICD manifest, like lavapipe.

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
